{
  "configuration_id": "config_007",
  "reason": "The current best is config_031 (scgpt + imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) at 0.542 acc. All four completed experiments use scgpt as the RNA encoder, so the RNA encoder is the largest untested design axis. config_007 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) is a clean single-variable swap of the RNA encoder while holding the best-performing image encoder (ViT-L), aggregation (avgpool), and fusion (weighted) fixed. This directly tests whether a different learned RNA representation can push accuracy above 0.542, which would open a new exploitation direction, or confirm that scgpt is near-optimal for this pipeline. Expected cost is comparable to config_031 (~3 GPU hours) since the architecture is nearly identical; scvi_n200 is a similar-scale learned encoder to scgpt. This is the highest-information experiment available: it resolves the biggest remaining uncertainty (RNA encoder choice) at low marginal cost, and with 5 experiments still remaining, a positive result would let us exploit the new encoder across other settings."
}

